WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.027
Welcome to Module 7 of the
Privileged Access learning path:

2
00:00:04.027 --> 00:00:06.462
access reviews of privileged roles.

3
00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:12.976
This module serves the project plan's
task A2.7 in Phase 2 and A3.7 in Phase 3,

4
00:00:12.976 --> 00:00:16.775
with Chapter 07 of the developer workbook.

5
00:00:16.775 --> 00:00:19.762
The approval gate controls
the use of privilege.

6
00:00:19.762 --> 00:00:22.712
Reviews control who keeps the eligibility.

7
00:00:22.712 --> 00:00:28.093
The program's design creates one recurring
review per role, Tier 0 monthly and the

8
00:00:28.093 --> 00:00:33.474
rest quarterly, with auto-apply on, and
remove access when reviewers don't respond.

9
00:00:33.474 --> 00:00:37.700
In this module you define every
privileged review series as code.

10
00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:41.782
You show a reviewer what a change
will do before it reaches the tenant,

11
00:00:41.782 --> 00:00:44.361
apply it with the least
permission that can,

12
00:00:44.361 --> 00:00:47.512
and hand the ISSO the
decisions each review produced.

13
00:00:47.512 --> 00:00:52.240
The code is illustrative: tested
against fixtures and a fake.

14
00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:56.840
Why code?

15
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.353
Because a review set up by hand drifts.

16
00:00:59.353 --> 00:01:02.117
A reviewer leaves, a
duration is shortened,

17
00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:05.828
auto-apply is switched off for
one cycle and never back on.

18
00:01:05.828 --> 00:01:07.852
And reviews have their own lockout.

19
00:01:07.852 --> 00:01:12.964
The emergency accounts hold Global
Administrator as permanent active assignments.

20
00:01:12.964 --> 00:01:18.069
A review of Global Administrator that
covers active assignments, with remove

21
00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:23.252
access on silence and auto-apply on, removes
them if the reviewers miss one month.

22
00:01:23.252 --> 00:01:26.798
Microsoft Learn's reference
for review settings cautions

23
00:01:26.798 --> 00:01:30.489
that auto-apply with a default
decision can revoke all access.

24
00:01:30.489 --> 00:01:34.708
So rule A R oh six fails a review
that would do that, and rule A R,

25
00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:38.840
E oh eight, reports an emergency
account a reviewer denied.

26
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.728
The apply refuses a plan with any finding.

27
00:01:41.728 --> 00:01:43.805
And the code never deletes a series,

28
00:01:43.805 --> 00:01:48.750
because deleting a definition deletes
its decisions, and those are evidence.

29
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.340
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

30
00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:57.987
which takes about fifty-five
minutes with the lab.

31
00:01:57.987 --> 00:02:02.875
You'll explain why privileged reviews belong
in code, and what licensing they need.

32
00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:07.063
You'll name the series the program
defines, and the cadence for each tier.

33
00:02:07.063 --> 00:02:12.050
You'll explain the A R oh six guard, and
why it changes the program's own setting.

34
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:15.370
You'll read a plan's
actions: Create, Update,

35
00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:18.787
Replace, NoChange, Unmanaged and Conflict.

36
00:02:18.787 --> 00:02:23.699
And you'll read the evidence
findings, A R, E oh one to E oh eight.

37
00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:25.995
Before you start, finish Module 2,

38
00:02:25.995 --> 00:02:30.415
for the emergency accounts that A
R oh six protects, and Module 5,

39
00:02:30.415 --> 00:02:35.175
for the P R V groups, each reviewed
through its own membership series.

40
00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:39.325
Lab 2 needs a worldwide or G
C C test tenant with Microsoft

41
00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:43.850
Entra I D Governance, a trial
will do, and never production.

42
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.587
Unit 1: why reviews, and the series.

43
00:02:50.587 --> 00:02:54.738
Seven series follow the program's
review schedule, in three kinds.

44
00:02:54.738 --> 00:02:58.126
Entra role series review
the users who hold a role,

45
00:02:58.126 --> 00:03:00.688
Tier 0 monthly and the rest quarterly.

46
00:03:00.688 --> 00:03:04.387
P R V group membership series
review each group's members;

47
00:03:04.387 --> 00:03:08.087
Microsoft Learn marks PIM for
Groups reviews as preview.

48
00:03:08.087 --> 00:03:11.563
And an Azure role series goes
through a preview A P I.

49
00:03:11.563 --> 00:03:13.587
A role series covers users.

50
00:03:13.587 --> 00:03:18.009
Groups that hold the role are reviewed
through their own membership series,

51
00:03:18.009 --> 00:03:20.676
and rule A R fourteen
flags a group without one.

52
00:03:20.676 --> 00:03:24.768
Licensing: the program budgets
Microsoft Entra I D Governance

53
00:03:24.768 --> 00:03:28.388
for every reviewer and every
reviewed privileged user.

54
00:03:28.388 --> 00:03:31.459
Microsoft Learn has two
licensing pages that differ,

55
00:03:31.459 --> 00:03:33.275
and that's the stricter reading.

56
00:03:33.275 --> 00:03:37.257
The monthly and quarterly cadence
is the program's own decision;

57
00:03:37.257 --> 00:03:40.550
NIST leaves the frequency
to the organization.

58
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:47.938
Unit 2: the checks, the
plan and the evidence.

59
00:03:47.938 --> 00:03:51.963
Rules A R oh one to fourteen check
each series before it's applied.

60
00:03:51.963 --> 00:03:54.525
Oh one is the first: no reviewers.

61
00:03:54.525 --> 00:03:59.544
Microsoft Learn's page on configuring
reviewers says Graph treats no reviewers

62
00:03:59.544 --> 00:04:03.963
as a self-review, and in this program
assignees never review themselves.

63
00:04:03.963 --> 00:04:05.936
Oh two is no fallback reviewer,

64
00:04:05.936 --> 00:04:09.962
and oh three a missing or over-long
description for reviewers.

65
00:04:09.962 --> 00:04:12.549
Oh four is a review longer than its cycle.

66
00:04:12.549 --> 00:04:14.413
Oh five is auto-apply off.

67
00:04:14.413 --> 00:04:16.238
Oh six is the lockout guard.

68
00:04:16.238 --> 00:04:18.787
And it changes the program's own setting:

69
00:04:18.787 --> 00:04:24.040
a review that covers the emergency accounts'
Global Administrator uses no change

70
00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:29.138
on silence, and an unreviewed item becomes
an evidence finding, E oh four, instead.

71
00:04:29.138 --> 00:04:30.801
That's the owner's decision.

72
00:04:30.801 --> 00:04:35.202
The rest check the default decision,
justification, the tier's cadence,

73
00:04:35.202 --> 00:04:39.908
the start date, reviewers on Azure
series, duplicate names, unlisted series,

74
00:04:39.908 --> 00:04:44.890
and a group that holds a reviewed role
with no membership series of its own.

75
00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:51.690
The plan compares the reviewed
file with the tenant.

76
00:04:51.690 --> 00:04:54.665
Create and Update are
sent, then read back.

77
00:04:54.665 --> 00:04:58.190
Replace is a scope change or
a change of group reviewers.

78
00:04:58.190 --> 00:05:03.446
Microsoft Learn's reference for updating
a definition says the update A P I doesn't

79
00:05:03.446 --> 00:05:06.692
take those, so a person
exports the series' evidence,

80
00:05:06.692 --> 00:05:09.165
deletes it in the portal, and runs again.

81
00:05:09.165 --> 00:05:10.578
NoChange does nothing.

82
00:05:10.578 --> 00:05:14.275
Unmanaged is a series in the
tenant the file doesn't list;

83
00:05:14.275 --> 00:05:16.365
it's reported, and never deleted.

84
00:05:16.365 --> 00:05:17.603
Then the evidence.

85
00:05:17.603 --> 00:05:21.992
Each decision becomes a row, and
eight checks find what went wrong:

86
00:05:21.992 --> 00:05:26.383
a missing series, an overdue instance,
a denial that wasn't applied,

87
00:05:26.383 --> 00:05:31.098
an item the no-response default decided,
an approval without a reason, a

88
00:05:31.098 --> 00:05:34.025
self-review, bulk
decisions by one reviewer,

89
00:05:34.025 --> 00:05:37.320
and an emergency account
a reviewer denied.

90
00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:41.795
Try it.

91
00:05:41.795 --> 00:05:45.208
Lab 1 runs in one PowerShell 7 session.

92
00:05:45.208 --> 00:05:48.758
Step one runs Microsoft
Learn's tutorial for reviewing

93
00:05:48.758 --> 00:05:52.770
access to administrative roles
against the fake, as published.

94
00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.320
Eleven tests pass.

95
00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.687
The third is the one to
notice: the tutorial's POST,

96
00:05:57.687 --> 00:06:00.970
sent twice, leaves two
series with the same name.

97
00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:05.695
That's why the code plans before it
writes, and why rule A R twelve exists.

98
00:06:05.695 --> 00:06:08.395
Step two lists each task's permissions.

99
00:06:08.395 --> 00:06:13.270
Planning needs Access Review dot Read
dot All, and Reader for the Azure series.

100
00:06:13.270 --> 00:06:18.908
Applying needs Access Review dot ReadWrite
dot All, and User Access Administrator.

101
00:06:18.908 --> 00:06:21.571
Reading the evidence needs
the same as planning.

102
00:06:21.571 --> 00:06:23.300
Write only to apply.

103
00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:29.262
Step three runs the dry run.

104
00:06:29.262 --> 00:06:35.101
One Create, two Updates, one Replace,
three NoChange and one Unmanaged.

105
00:06:35.101 --> 00:06:39.488
The checks: no findings, one
warning, one information item.

106
00:06:39.488 --> 00:06:42.676
Nothing is sent; two writes
would be sent with Apply.

107
00:06:42.676 --> 00:06:44.325
Step four reads the diff.

108
00:06:44.325 --> 00:06:49.987
The Tier 0 Global Administrator series is
an Update: its instance duration changes.

109
00:06:49.987 --> 00:06:54.438
The Privileged Role Administrator
series doesn't exist yet: Create.

110
00:06:54.438 --> 00:06:58.258
The Exchange Administrator
series changes its reviewers,

111
00:06:58.258 --> 00:07:00.363
so it's a Replace, left for a person.

112
00:07:00.363 --> 00:07:02.800
Three P R V group series match.

113
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:07.628
The Azure Owner series is an Update too,
but it goes through a preview A P I,

114
00:07:07.628 --> 00:07:12.375
so it needs the Include Preview switch;
that's why only two writes count.

115
00:07:12.375 --> 00:07:15.760
And a Security Administrator
series in the tenant

116
00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.500
isn't in the file:
Unmanaged, never deleted.

117
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:22.880
The bodies folder holds each
request body for a reviewer to read.

118
00:07:26.630 --> 00:07:31.667
Step five checks the body from Microsoft
Learn's tutorial with the example's rules.

119
00:07:31.667 --> 00:07:36.129
It fails three: A R oh two, no
fallback reviewer; oh three,

120
00:07:36.129 --> 00:07:40.793
no description for reviewers;
and oh five, auto-apply off.

121
00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:45.675
And it warns twice: oh seven, the
no-response default isn't Deny,

122
00:07:45.675 --> 00:07:48.506
and ten, its start date is in the past.

123
00:07:48.506 --> 00:07:53.492
Step six applies in the fake, the same
command as the dry run, with Apply.

124
00:07:53.492 --> 00:07:56.987
Two writes are sent: the Global
Administrator update and

125
00:07:56.987 --> 00:08:00.555
the Privileged Role Administrator
create, each read back.

126
00:08:00.555 --> 00:08:03.155
Everything else is
skipped, with the reason.

127
00:08:03.155 --> 00:08:06.306
The Replace needs a person:
export its evidence,

128
00:08:06.306 --> 00:08:08.730
delete it in the portal, and run again.

129
00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:11.192
The three P R V series match.

130
00:08:11.192 --> 00:08:13.630
The Azure update needs Include Preview.

131
00:08:13.630 --> 00:08:16.480
And the unmanaged series is never deleted.

132
00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:19.180
The slide condenses the two tables.

133
00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:27.646
Step seven reads the evidence:
eighteen decisions in seven instances,

134
00:08:27.646 --> 00:08:30.167
with seven findings and two warnings.

135
00:08:30.167 --> 00:08:34.867
E oh one: the Privileged Role Administrator
series isn't in the tenant yet.

136
00:08:34.867 --> 00:08:37.732
E oh two: the Tier 0 Global Administrator

137
00:08:37.732 --> 00:08:40.943
group's series has no
closed instance in time.

138
00:08:40.943 --> 00:08:45.588
E oh eight: a reviewer denied
Emergency Access 02 in October,

139
00:08:45.588 --> 00:08:48.717
the finding this module exists to catch.

140
00:08:48.717 --> 00:08:54.309
E oh four: an item nobody reviewed,
decided by the no-response default;

141
00:08:54.309 --> 00:08:57.305
a finding on Tier 0, a warning on Tier 1.

142
00:08:57.305 --> 00:09:00.743
E oh five: an approval
without a justification.

143
00:09:00.743 --> 00:09:04.229
E oh three: a denial whose
result wasn't applied.

144
00:09:04.229 --> 00:09:07.405
E oh six: someone reviewed
their own access.

145
00:09:07.405 --> 00:09:12.763
And E oh seven: one reviewer recorded a
run of identical decisions within minutes,

146
00:09:12.763 --> 00:09:16.410
the bulk-decision check
from the program's design.

147
00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.222
Step eight shows the lockout guard.

148
00:09:22.222 --> 00:09:25.261
Load the reviewed file,
and change one thing:

149
00:09:25.261 --> 00:09:30.072
set the Tier 0 Global Administrator
series' default decision to Deny.

150
00:09:30.072 --> 00:09:33.635
Then build a client that
may write, plan, and apply.

151
00:09:33.635 --> 00:09:36.326
It refuses: the plan has one finding,

152
00:09:36.326 --> 00:09:39.760
A R oh six, on the Global
Administrator series.

153
00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:40.935
Nothing is sent.

154
00:09:40.935 --> 00:09:42.724
If the reviewers missed a month,

155
00:09:42.724 --> 00:09:47.198
that review would have removed the
emergency accounts' Global Administrator.

156
00:09:47.198 --> 00:09:50.271
Step nine runs the tests,
three hundred thirty pass,

157
00:09:50.271 --> 00:09:55.160
and you delete the output folder,
because the evidence folder names people.

158
00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:04.519
Lab 2 runs in a worldwide or G C C test
tenant with Microsoft Entra I D Governance,

159
00:10:04.519 --> 00:10:09.697
a trial will do, and for the optional
Azure step, a test Azure subscription.

160
00:10:09.697 --> 00:10:10.823
Never production.

161
00:10:10.823 --> 00:10:16.261
Pick a role with no real holders, such as
Reports Reader, not Global Administrator.

162
00:10:16.261 --> 00:10:21.010
Register a reader app and an applier
app, write a test file with one series,

163
00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:25.522
dry-run as the reader, and apply after
a second person reads the bodies.

164
00:10:25.522 --> 00:10:29.560
Then close one instance as a test
reviewer, and read the evidence.

165
00:10:29.560 --> 00:10:34.202
The reader gets Access Review dot Read
dot All, the applier Access Review dot

166
00:10:34.202 --> 00:10:39.360
ReadWrite dot All, and User Access Administrator
only for the optional Azure series.

167
00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:41.832
The back-out exports the evidence first,

168
00:10:41.832 --> 00:10:46.777
then deletes the test series in the admin
center, because the code never deletes,

169
00:10:46.777 --> 00:10:50.448
along with the apps, their
certificates and the test groups.

170
00:10:50.448 --> 00:10:52.970
The authors haven't run Lab 2.

171
00:10:56.720 --> 00:10:58.107
The federal requirement.

172
00:10:58.107 --> 00:11:01.861
The review series and
their decisions are the

173
00:11:01.861 --> 00:11:05.121
evidence for the plan's
tasks A2.7 and A3.7.

174
00:11:05.121 --> 00:11:11.022
From NIST special publication eight
hundred fifty-three they support A C six,

175
00:11:11.022 --> 00:11:16.187
enhancement seven, review of user
privileges; A C two, account review;

176
00:11:16.187 --> 00:11:20.245
A C five, separation of duties;
and A U eleven, retention.

177
00:11:20.245 --> 00:11:25.666
A C six, enhancement seven, and A C two
leave the frequency to the organization;

178
00:11:25.666 --> 00:11:28.850
monthly for Tier 0 and
quarterly for the rest

179
00:11:28.850 --> 00:11:32.120
is the program's own
decision, design guidance.

180
00:11:32.120 --> 00:11:36.795
The evidence an ISSO keeps: the
reviewed file and each plan's bodies;

181
00:11:36.795 --> 00:11:42.320
each apply's results; and each evidence
run's decisions, instances and findings,

182
00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.350
in the access-controlled evidence
store, because they name people.

183
00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:53.075
Check yourself with two questions.

184
00:11:53.075 --> 00:11:57.610
First: a Global Administrator
review covers active assignments,

185
00:11:57.610 --> 00:12:00.213
with Deny on silence and auto-apply on.

186
00:12:00.213 --> 00:12:01.849
What does A R oh six do?

187
00:12:01.849 --> 00:12:05.225
The answer is b: it fails the
review, because missing one

188
00:12:05.225 --> 00:12:09.350
month would remove the emergency
accounts' Global Administrator.

189
00:12:09.350 --> 00:12:11.500
You saw it in Lab 1, step eight.

190
00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:14.663
Second: the plan shows
a series as Replace.

191
00:12:14.663 --> 00:12:16.338
What does the apply do with it?

192
00:12:16.338 --> 00:12:18.575
The answer is b: it skips it.

193
00:12:18.575 --> 00:12:22.898
The update A P I doesn't take a
new scope or new group reviewers,

194
00:12:22.898 --> 00:12:26.875
so a person exports the series'
evidence and replaces it.

195
00:12:26.875 --> 00:12:28.525
You saw it in step six.

196
00:12:28.525 --> 00:12:33.780
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.

197
00:12:37.530 --> 00:12:38.355
To sum up.

198
00:12:38.355 --> 00:12:42.050
You planned seven review series
against a fictional tenant,

199
00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:45.079
saw Learn's tutorial body
fail the program's rules,

200
00:12:45.079 --> 00:12:49.734
applied two writes and left the Replace
and the unmanaged series to a person,

201
00:12:49.734 --> 00:12:52.468
read eighteen decisions
and their findings,

202
00:12:52.468 --> 00:12:57.567
and saw the lockout guard refuse a review
that would remove the emergency accounts.

203
00:12:57.567 --> 00:13:04.117
Next is Module 8: evidence and drift for
the ISSO, the last module of the path.

204
00:13:04.117 --> 00:13:06.652
You run the privileged
reads on a schedule,

205
00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:11.287
say what changed since the last run
without putting anyone's name in the issue

206
00:13:11.287 --> 00:13:14.112
tracker, and hand the ISSO
a package and a period

207
00:13:14.112 --> 00:13:16.860
summary they can check
with a hash tool alone.
